00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.240
So, I believe, the next one he put in

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:01.550
was the Black Panther beating up the KKK.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:02.627
So, that's what he did.

00:11:02.627 --> 00:11:04.080
But we have to fact check that one.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:04.965
We have to fact check that.

00:11:04.965 --> 00:11:06.900
- Black Panther's first
appearance was what?

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.460
In "Fantastic Four?"

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.490
Did I nail that?

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.323
Let's go.
- Yeah.

00:11:10.323 --> 00:11:11.920
- Okay.
- Anyway, it's something.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:13.497
- Why'd you write this book?
- Why'd I write this book?

00:11:13.497 --> 00:11:14.600
- You were under contract

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:15.969
and you need to bang 'em out?
- No.

00:11:15.969 --> 00:11:16.802
- No, that's good.
- No, no, no, no, no.

00:11:16.802 --> 00:11:17.635
It's extremely hard.

00:11:17.635 --> 00:11:18.870
I'm dyslexic.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.760
And, you know, so I wrote
this book because it was about

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:26.280
one week that I got, as we
all get our things from people

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:27.770
all the time, and they
were asking me how to

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.730
create change in their lives.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:30.997
And I've seen you say it often.

00:11:30.997 --> 00:11:32.137
"You're not gonna do anything right

00:11:32.137 --> 00:11:33.100
"after I tell you this."

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:33.985
Right?
- Yeah.

00:11:33.985 --> 00:11:34.818
- Most of them, right?

00:11:34.818 --> 00:11:37.397
And they were all using
and masking it with,

00:11:37.397 --> 00:11:38.230
"Well, here's my job.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.063
"Here's this and that."

00:11:39.063 --> 00:11:40.740
you know, Warren Buffet said
something really amazing.

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.760
You may go throughout
various aspects of your life,

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.150
but the only thing that you are

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.930
fully in control of is yourself.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.980
And I realized that people
just didn't understand

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.660
what they can do today to make them better

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:53.840
for tomorrow and the next
day and the next day.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.010
And it was all about negotiation.

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:59.940
I think the thing that
makes me or somebody else

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.630
more successful, let's
just say, it's all of

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:04.100
the aspects of what we negotiated in life.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:05.640
First of all, with ourselves.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.950
Second of all, with the
surrounding and the families

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.350
or whatever the case is.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.070
Third of all, with our position.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:14.200
Listen, I was born Black.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.190
That's not gonna change.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:17.990
I'm not gonna be Chinese,
white, or yellow tomorrow.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:20.380
That is what it is, and that's what it is.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.910
Get over it, move forward,
use it as an asset

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.470
in any place that I can,
whatever the case is.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.380
So, people always thought that negotiation

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.560
and those things of that
nature to create change

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.960
is either you having all
the power or somebody else

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:36.200
taking the power from you or
they gotta give it to you.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.190
And it's not that way.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.760
- Which leads to deep unhappiness.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:39.593
- [Daymond] Exactly.

00:12:39.593 --> 00:12:41.350
- The second you think
somebody else is in control,

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:42.930
you're in big trouble.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.180
- When somebody else is in
control of your destiny,

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:45.013
you're in big trouble.

00:12:45.013 --> 00:12:46.550
But--
- I think about this a lot,

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:49.090
and obviously it falls into
race and gender issues,

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.650
but I actually think about
it in parenting dynamics.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:52.690
So much.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:53.600
- And it happens when,

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:54.980
and this is a three part.

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:58.230
You have to build influence,
you have to then negotiate,

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:01.640
and you have to nurture
a long relationship

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.300
because this part of the relationship

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.600
where you just had created
some kind of value,

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.880
is nothing in comparison to here.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.310
And it has to all be concise,

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:11.710
and I don't think people understand that.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:13.270
So, if somebody said,

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.140
if I'm in an elevator with Gary Vee

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:15.973
I never thought I would see Gary.

00:13:15.973 --> 00:13:17.080
He was in Oklahoma.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.510
I never thought I would
see Gary Vee in my life.

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:20.110
How'm I gonna build influence with him

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.670
when I got 90 seconds?

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.650
Listen, first of all, make sure the pitch

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.010
you say really quick is, you know,

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.280
what's in it for Gary.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:28.900
How you've been doing really well with it.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:30.380
And the fact that you're
gonna be successful

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.190
with or without him or
not, but if you have,

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:35.400
if you can offer some
opportunity to him, let him know.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:37.390
Your influence is when Gary and his team

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.450
is gonna go back and look at
the shit you've been saying

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.500
for the last 10 years on social media.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.690
Good, bad, or indifferent.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:46.840
They're either gonna say, I
want this person around me.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.880
or I don't want this person around me.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.210
And it's not just you.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.640
You're hanging out with
this person right here,

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.410
who you would never bring to Gary's office

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.890
because he's a alcoholic or
a misogynist or racist pig.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:13:59.460
Stop taking pictures with him,

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.640
posting them all over your site,

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.290
'cause Gary's not just looking there.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:03.627
Gary's looking everywhere around you,

00:14:03.627 --> 00:14:06.080
and people don't understand how important

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.510
the influence was that
they had to build prior

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:13.360
to then negotiating and then
valuing the relationship.

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.160
And it's just simple stuff.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:15.993
Simple stuff.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.533
- Simple when it's quiet in one's head.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:21.983
Right?

00:14:21.983 --> 00:14:22.816
Like, I've been thinking a lot about this.

00:14:22.816 --> 00:14:24.040
Like, I wanted to ask you this.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.233
How quiet and slow are things for you?

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.160
I've been thinking, and
here's how I'm saying it.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.550
Like, you hear athletes talk about

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.210
when the game slows down.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:35.090
- [Daymond] Yeah.

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:38.600
- I'm manic in my schedule,
and like, you know,

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.450
I'm also an extrovert by nature,

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:43.380
and so there's a lot of things
that go on with my energy,

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:45.900
and I wish there was a way
that I could explain to people

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:48.310
how slow everything feels to me.

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:49.380
- [Daymond] Same here.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.436
- Good, I'm glad.

00:14:50.436 --> 00:14:51.597
I thought that might make sense.

00:14:51.597 --> 00:14:53.100
- Yeah, but that's why we see each other

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.420
on the road so much, and
people ask why we do it.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:57.259
Why shouldn't I do it, you know?

00:14:57.259 --> 00:14:59.620
- First of all, if you like it,
that's really the best part.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.450
- I'm tweaking my life
and I'm making sure that,

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:04.610
all right, family needs to come out here,

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.420
I need to spend more time here,

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:07.440
I need to do more at this office,

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:09.800
I need more great people around me.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.160
A lotta more Robins.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.460
So I'm Batman and they're Robin.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:14.520
They're Robin, I'm Batman half the time.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.740
I need more of them
'cause I'm not gonna die,

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.573
I'm not going anywhere.

00:15:17.573 --> 00:15:18.660
What am I gonna do?

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.000
And I'm educating myself
while I'm out there.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.540
I'm expanding my network.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.270
- Can you explain to the kids out here

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:27.860
