00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:03.910
She changed the face of like, women.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:05.220
- Women in sports, right?

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.020
So, this is obviously,
you were in my last book.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.580
I only take subjects out
that I can learn from

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:12.070
on the same path as you are in this.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.770
You know, when I'm talking to
somebody about negotiation,

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:16.120
a lot of people don't
realize this is really easy

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.710
because of social media.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:19.070
People talk in five different ways,

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:19.903
and they communicate five different ways.

00:18:19.903 --> 00:18:22.010
There's the sight, sound,

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:24.530
sight, sound, touch, taste, and smell.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:25.550
And it's very simple.

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:26.570
If you're on social media,

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:28.260
you can look through peoples' feeds,

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:29.630
and you wanna talk to them.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:30.930
It's like a used car salesman.

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:32.570
Used car salesman, you walk into the room,

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:33.790
he starts to listen,

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:36.090
or she starts to listen to
how you're communicating.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.340
All right, there's a red Corvette there,

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.500
it has the top down.

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:39.367
If you're about sight, he goes,

00:18:39.367 --> 00:18:40.707
"Can you see yourself
driving down the road,

00:18:40.707 --> 00:18:43.620
"looking at the leaves
falling on a winding road?"

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:44.557
And if you're about smelling, he's like,

00:18:44.557 --> 00:18:46.427
"Can you smell the rich leather?"

00:18:46.427 --> 00:18:48.330
"Can you smell the air in the crisp air?"

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:51.767
If you're about sound, "Can
you hear the engine roaring?"

00:18:51.767 --> 00:18:53.017
- That makes sense.
- You see?

00:18:53.017 --> 00:18:54.847
And there's various ways of communication,

00:18:54.847 --> 00:18:57.070
and you see us do it all
the time with "Shark Tank,"

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:01.760
'cause 65% of communication,
you know, is body language.

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:04.260
Only 7% is exactly what you're saying,

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:05.870
and the rest is how you said it, right.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.700
And there's various
different ways to indicate

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:09.230
and go through a negotiation.

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:12.230
That's why when I get deals,
I can see when the person

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:13.130
putting their hand in their pocket,

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.060
putting their hair over their ear,

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.840
Robert sitting up and he closes his book.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:18.340
You know, what's the name?

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.030
Kevin O'Leary always
wants to put something

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:22.440
in between you to create the distance.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:24.180
And there's a lot of
information in this book

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:27.210
of keys on ways to
communicate, build influence,

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:28.300
and then nurture that relationship

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.891
to get way more after that.

00:19:29.891 --> 00:19:30.724
