- Rodney!

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:37.333
All right.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.390
- Yeah, that's interesting.

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:42.463
So, you think that there's a lot of--

00:19:42.463 --> 00:19:44.250
- [Daymond] There's a lot
of nuggets in this book

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.590
that you take away two
and three or four of them,

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:48.720
they just helped you close one deal.

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:50.777
- One deal's are why positive.

00:19:50.777 --> 00:19:52.950
(line trilling)

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:54.080
- They let you get the remote control

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.630
away from your wife or husband.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:58.483
- [Rodney] Hello.

00:19:58.483 --> 00:19:59.316
- Rodney?

00:20:00.151 --> 00:20:01.420
- [Rodney] May I ask who's, yes?

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:02.253
- It's Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:20:02.253 --> 00:20:03.960
You're on with Daymond John.

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.050
- [Rodney] Gary Vee, how you doing?

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.210
Daymond John, how you doing?

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:08.190
- I'm great.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:09.138
What's happenin' Rodney?
- Rodney, where you from?

00:20:09.138 --> 00:20:09.971
- [Rodney] I'm over here.

00:20:09.971 --> 00:20:11.150
I'm from Miami, Florida.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:11.983
- Let's go.

00:20:11.983 --> 00:20:13.020
- [Rodney] But I'm livin'
in Atlanta right now.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:13.853
- Oh I love it.

00:20:13.853 --> 00:20:15.550
- [Rodney] And I'm
listening to you on LinkedIn

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:16.383
And you called me.

00:20:16.383 --> 00:20:17.678
I was not expecting to sit up.

00:20:17.678 --> 00:20:19.073
- Well, you put your
phone number on LinkedIn,

00:20:19.073 --> 00:20:20.590
so it worked out.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:21.660
- [Rodney] Hey, nothing much.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.628
Hey, yeah, yeah, I got
a question for you man.

00:20:24.628 --> 00:20:26.880
And I see that you and your brother

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:28.930
have your agency going on right now.

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:32.140
I'm pursuing my Master's
to become a sports agent.

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:34.700
Looking forward to that by the end,

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:36.460
by the beginning of next year

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.940
to be a certified sports agent.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:42.487
What advice would you have
for a young guy like me,

00:20:42.487 --> 00:20:44.110
entering that field there?

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:46.020
I got a background of playing football,

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.237
have friends in the NFL right now.

00:20:48.237 --> 00:20:50.150
But for me starting out, you know,

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:53.170
being so close to the game,
what advice would you give to me

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:55.050
to become a successful sports agent?

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.550
- Let me give you my
take, and then Daymond,

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:57.760
see if you can fill out some spots.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.310
So, the biggest thing I've learned,

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:00.340
AJ's been in the business now

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.210
for four years, VaynerSports.

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.210
The biggest thing that's really honest,

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:07.410
is that it's a lot more
simple than you think.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.080
Like, I keep watching us lose,

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.470
let me go a different route.

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:14.700
The players that we
lose to other agencies,

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:17.790
where we're offering disproportionate

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:21.310
more impact financially
and infrastructure-wise,

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:25.550
strictly because that player liked

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.250
a different agent more than the agent

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.380
we put in front of them, whether that's AJ

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:32.370
or Brandon Parker or Tommy or Brian,

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:34.260
you will be blown away, my man,

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:37.843
of how much of this is
strictly being liked.

00:21:39.363 --> 00:21:40.330
- [Rodney] Strictly being liked.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:41.630
- You will be blown,

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:42.920
you're gonna go into this business

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.280
and be discouraged 'cause
you're gonna be like,

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:45.780
wait, the five biggest firms,

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.060
back to what Daymond said,

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:48.690
he's not gonna change that he was Black.

00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:50.630
I'm not gonna change that I started at,

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.520
that I was not athletically inclined

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:54.910
or educationally inclined,
which made everybody

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.530
from the '70s and '80s feel like shit,

00:21:56.530 --> 00:21:59.133
for the first 18 years of your life.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.270
That doesn't change.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:04.330
And I'll tell you this,
when you get into the game,

00:22:04.330 --> 00:22:06.560
if you start small or a small firm,

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:08.300
you're gonna go what every agent does,

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.630
which is like woe is me.

00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:10.970
It's CA, it's Roc Nation.

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:12.840
By the time you get into
it, we're like, on our way.

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:14.520
We have 13 guys in this draft.

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:15.353
It's been written.

00:22:15.353 --> 00:22:16.560
We're gonna be a player.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:19.290
But the reality is, I'm watching people

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:22.060
strictly pick people on likability,

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:23.130
nothing else.

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:24.380
Not what they can do.

00:22:24.380 --> 00:22:25.770
Like, plenty of people go to Roc Nation

00:22:25.770 --> 00:22:27.300
because they want their selfie with Jay-Z.

00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:28.620
Plenty of people go to VaynerSports

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:30.910
'cause they want business
and life after football

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:32.020
and off the field stuff.

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:33.360
Plenty of people go to Athletes First

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:35.890
'cause Mulugheta's a great
agent and they built a thing.

00:22:35.890 --> 00:22:38.020
There's a lot of places where people go.

00:22:38.020 --> 00:22:39.500
I am stunned.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:42.270
And I mean stunned, on how many people go

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:44.407
with a person they liked the most.

00:22:44.407 --> 00:22:45.240
Liked.

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:46.330
- [Rodney] Right, and so--

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:47.163
But...

00:22:48.852 --> 00:22:50.310
No, so right.

00:22:50.310 --> 00:22:52.060
I'm a very likable guy.

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:54.260
I get along with a lot of people, man.

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:55.860
- Well, good news.

00:22:55.860 --> 00:22:57.287
Good, good news.

00:22:57.287 --> 00:23:00.070
Real quick and then I'll let
you jump in Jimmy, Daymond.

00:23:00.070 --> 00:23:01.340
Good news.

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:04.530
You're gonna talk yourself
out of all the things.

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:06.090
You're gonna talk about
all these other things

00:23:06.090 --> 00:23:07.647
that you need to do.

00:23:07.647 --> 00:23:08.957
"Oh, we need to get marketing right.

00:23:08.957 --> 00:23:10.467
"We need to be social media right.

00:23:10.467 --> 00:23:11.867
"I gotta get some of my homies I played

00:23:11.867 --> 00:23:12.850
"with football co-sign."

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:15.030
you're gonna think of
a million other things

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:16.730
that you're gonna learn matter,

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:19.520
and I'm telling you 50
fucking percent of it

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:21.820
is do human beings like you?

00:23:21.820 --> 00:23:24.530
And if you actually
lean into that mentally,

00:23:24.530 --> 00:23:26.730
you're gonna get real happy
'cause you're gonna realize

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:28.220
that you don't have to
work on all these things

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:29.576
that you think you have to work on.

00:23:29.576 --> 00:23:30.409
Daymond.

00:23:30.409 --> 00:23:31.242
- Yeah, I mean, I think
it's about the same thing.

00:23:31.242 --> 00:23:33.470
You know, you gotta go narrow
and deep on your targets

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:35.230
that you want, and like he was saying,

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:36.410
you're gonna go everywhere.

00:23:36.410 --> 00:23:38.193
But I think, also, the
co-signing of the people

00:23:38.193 --> 00:23:40.670
that you already know,
that really do like you,

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:41.910
you could tell us you're likable,

00:23:41.910 --> 00:23:44.560
but everybody's gonna be on
their first date telling you,

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:46.520
you know, your baby's beautiful, right?

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:47.700
Or they're beautiful.

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:51.180
You gotta dig deep into your database

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:54.250
and go after one, two
key players that like you

00:23:54.250 --> 00:23:56.680
and that you like, and that
you can bring value to,

00:23:56.680 --> 00:24:00.313
and just keep having these other
people also co-signing you.

00:24:00.313 --> 00:24:02.030
Like he said, you're gonna
try to get all the people.

00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:04.270
Just get one or two
people that really, really

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:07.100
mess with you to dig deep,
and you gotta, of course,

00:24:07.100 --> 00:24:08.620
be out there doing your
homework and be ready

00:24:08.620 --> 00:24:10.860
to pound the phones for
those cats, and let them

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:13.520
see that you're ready to just
put in the hours, you know?

00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:14.690
- I'll give you two more insights

00:24:14.690 --> 00:24:15.640
'cause I really want you to win.

00:24:15.640 --> 00:24:17.840
One, everybody matters.

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:19.140
I went through this whole thing of like,

00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:21.420
the parents matter, the
parents don't matter.

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:23.760
You know, the uncle matters,
the uncle doesn't matter.

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:25.630
The trainer matters, the
trainer doesn't matter.

00:24:25.630 --> 00:24:27.750
The coach matters, but here's the rule.

00:24:27.750 --> 00:24:29.310
- Everybody matters.
- Every fucking person matters

00:24:29.310 --> 00:24:31.440
'cause we're influencing,
these are young kids.

00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:35.530
And then finally, complete
and utter detachment.

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:36.830
You're gonna get your heart broke.

00:24:36.830 --> 00:24:39.000
Some kid's gonna tell you you're his guy

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.900
all the way through, all the way through,

00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:44.150
all the way through,
and then it's gonna come

00:24:44.150 --> 00:24:45.527
to signing day and they're gonna call you

00:24:45.527 --> 00:24:47.427
and be like, "Yeah, I'm
going with this other firm.

00:24:47.427 --> 00:24:49.190
"I'm sorry, see ya."

00:24:49.190 --> 00:24:51.070
- [Rodney] I've heard
those stories already.

00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:53.670
Gary Vee, I was up there at
the Alabama Reese's Bowl game.

00:24:53.670 --> 00:24:55.570
I was definitely looking for you.

00:24:55.570 --> 00:24:58.680
I was trying my hardest
to look for you out there.

00:24:58.680 --> 00:25:00.920
Saw you, saw you pulling
up out there on the field,

00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:03.810
as I was leaving Alabama,
driving back to Atlanta.

00:25:03.810 --> 00:25:05.340
But Daymond, I got a
question for you as well.

00:25:05.340 --> 00:25:06.710
If I can shoot this
out there really quick.

00:25:06.710 --> 00:25:07.697
- [Gary] Go quick.

00:25:07.697 --> 00:25:10.560
- [Rodney] Would you say that
FUBU could make a comeback?

00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:11.920
Would you bring FUBU back out?

00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:13.840
A lot of people, this is in the south,

00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:15.530
a brand, like Gary talks about,

00:25:15.530 --> 00:25:19.550
but where can we see FUBU in the future?

00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:21.070
- Yeah, you can go to
fubu.com and get that.

00:25:21.070 --> 00:25:22.410
Yeah, it can make a comeback.

00:25:22.410 --> 00:25:24.570
It all depends on how
much energy that I want

00:25:24.570 --> 00:25:26.100
to put into it, and I have other partners

00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:27.957
that have been putting energy into it,

00:25:27.957 --> 00:25:29.320
but it absolutely can make a comeback.

00:25:29.320 --> 00:25:31.060
It won't be on the same
platform as before,

00:25:31.060 --> 00:25:31.893
just in retail.

00:25:31.893 --> 00:25:34.020
It probably should be
a subscription service

00:25:34.020 --> 00:25:35.530
or one of those things.

00:25:35.530 --> 00:25:37.960
And absolutely, there's a
lot of content out there,

00:25:37.960 --> 00:25:39.830
there's a lot of history,
it's a global brand.

00:25:39.830 --> 00:25:41.940
But we need to get our ducks in order too.

00:25:41.940 --> 00:25:43.420
- Thanks for the question.
- I got ya.

00:25:43.420 --> 00:25:46.150
- Yeah, I mean, what
an iconic brand it is,

00:25:46.150 --> 00:25:47.100
and I'm with you on that.

00:25:47.100 --> 00:25:48.703
All right, let's get another one in.

00:25:49.642 --> 00:25:52.450
Yeah, man, I'm shocked how much these kids

00:25:52.450 --> 00:25:55.430
are smarter than ever but yet,

00:25:55.430 --> 00:25:58.500
there's one kid who's
logically talked me through,

00:25:58.500 --> 00:26:01.500
why we were disproportionally
right for him,

00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:03.067
and then he said, "But
I'm going with another guy

00:26:03.067 --> 00:26:04.207
"'cause it was love at first sight."

00:26:04.207 --> 00:26:05.540
- [Kasari] Hello.

00:26:05.540 --> 00:26:06.790
- Who's this?

00:26:06.790 --> 00:26:08.324
- Kas, Kasari?

00:26:08.324 --> 00:26:09.157
- [Kasari] Kasari.

00:26:09.157 --> 00:26:10.553
- Kasari.
- Kasari, what's good?

00:26:10.553 --> 00:26:12.728
- [Kasari] Hey, yo, Gary
Vee, my man, what's going on?

00:26:12.728 --> 00:26:13.757
And Daymond, what's up?
- What's happening?

00:26:13.757 --> 00:26:15.840
- [Kasari] Holy smokes,
man, I'm truly humbled

00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:17.500
to even be talking to you guys right now.

00:26:17.500 --> 00:26:18.640
Seriously.
- It's an honor.

00:26:18.640 --> 00:26:20.420
- Thank you Kasari.

00:26:20.420 --> 00:26:22.325
- [Kasari] Yo, so, my
question is, you know,

00:26:22.325 --> 00:26:25.970
it's pretty simple but it's
pretty complicated, as well.

00:26:25.970 --> 00:26:27.570
So right now, I live in Brooklyn,

00:26:27.570 --> 00:26:31.800
I live with my mom and my
sister and my twin brother.

00:26:31.800 --> 00:26:33.864
Three of us live in one single room.

00:26:33.864 --> 00:26:34.697
- Rough.

00:26:34.697 --> 00:26:37.027
- [Kasari] You know, so, it's
pretty challenging, you know.

00:26:37.027 --> 00:26:39.090
And I have a passion.
- How old are you?

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:39.923
- I'm 22.

00:26:39.923 --> 00:26:41.170
- Ooh.
- Keep going.

00:26:41.170 --> 00:26:44.040
- [Kasari] I'm 22, I
just graduated school,

00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:47.840
so I'm trying to figure out
life right now so I know what,

00:26:47.840 --> 00:26:51.091
I 100% know that I want to go
into real estate investing.

00:26:51.091 --> 00:26:53.140
That's really where I
see like, my business.

00:26:53.140 --> 00:26:54.950
- Why?
- You know, going into it.

00:26:54.950 --> 00:26:56.230
- Why?
- Simply because I feel like

00:26:56.230 --> 00:26:59.040
I can connect a lot of people and also,

00:26:59.040 --> 00:27:02.270
the first time not having
a home where I can really

00:27:02.270 --> 00:27:05.970
just kind of be myself and kind of expand.

00:27:05.970 --> 00:27:08.330
That's really also something
that I just kind of,

00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:10.110
you know, I wanna be
able to give other people

00:27:10.110 --> 00:27:13.420
that opportunity in order to, you know,

00:27:13.420 --> 00:27:15.467
have a nice place to live.

00:27:15.467 --> 00:27:16.300
- Makes sense.
- So, right now,

00:27:16.300 --> 00:27:17.993
I feel like the biggest struggle
for me has been, you know,

00:27:17.993 --> 00:27:20.300
it's pretty much the energy, I guess,

00:27:20.300 --> 00:27:22.340
like, in the house in a way.

00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:23.690
So, just trying to figure out

00:27:23.690 --> 00:27:25.670
what is it that I can do just to kind of

00:27:25.670 --> 00:27:26.503
be at my best self.

00:27:26.503 --> 00:27:27.900
'Cause back in school, you know, I was

00:27:27.900 --> 00:27:29.770
crushin' it left and right, you know.

00:27:29.770 --> 00:27:32.430
I was pretty much manifesting
everything that I wanted to,

00:27:32.430 --> 00:27:34.532
and now I feel like it's
hard for me to take action.

00:27:34.532 --> 00:27:35.365
- Why?

00:27:36.317 --> 00:27:39.680
- [Kasari] I just feel like
it's the negative influences

00:27:39.680 --> 00:27:42.150
of my parents and stuff like that.

00:27:42.150 --> 00:27:43.520
- Why are you still home?

00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:45.670
Is it that you're taking
care of your parents?

00:27:45.670 --> 00:27:49.420
Are they disabled or anything like that?

00:27:49.420 --> 00:27:50.270
'Cause you're 22.

00:27:51.120 --> 00:27:52.610
- [Kasari] Well, so, the reason why

00:27:52.610 --> 00:27:54.470
is New York's real expensive stuff.

00:27:54.470 --> 00:27:56.170
Trying to save a bit of money.

00:27:56.170 --> 00:27:58.410
- [Kasari] Just the kind
of, you know, stay at home

00:27:58.410 --> 00:28:01.677
for as long as I could,
but right now, like I was--

00:28:01.677 --> 00:28:03.587
- But have you--
- I'll let you, yeah.

00:28:03.587 --> 00:28:05.690
- No, I'm sorry, please finish.

00:28:05.690 --> 00:28:07.500
- [Kasari] Yeah, no, I was
actually debating, you know,

00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:09.890
whether or not I should go
ahead and rent out an apartment.

00:28:09.890 --> 00:28:11.270
Like, I know I would be rushing.

00:28:11.270 --> 00:28:12.180
- I mean, it's really interesting.

00:28:12.180 --> 00:28:14.090
It almost feels like
you're having a logical

00:28:14.090 --> 00:28:15.870
and an emotional
conversation with yourself,

00:28:15.870 --> 00:28:17.280
which I think we all do.

00:28:17.280 --> 00:28:19.660
I love that you're thinking about saving,

00:28:19.660 --> 00:28:21.870
and you have the humility
at 22 to be in your home,

00:28:21.870 --> 00:28:23.260
which I love.

00:28:23.260 --> 00:28:25.836
Are you also in a place where,

00:28:25.836 --> 00:28:28.930
are your parents negative by nature?

00:28:28.930 --> 00:28:31.460
Like, is that fucking you up?

00:28:31.460 --> 00:28:33.430
- [Kasari] Yeah, so, look,
really where it's ending.

00:28:33.430 --> 00:28:35.670
That my mom and my dad separated

00:28:35.670 --> 00:28:37.950
when I was super young,
so my mom has been,

00:28:37.950 --> 00:28:40.482
she put four kids through
college by herself.

00:28:40.482 --> 00:28:41.315
- Beast.
